WEBVTT

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:12.370
Breathing out as I sink to the bottom...

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.370
I breathe out,

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:17.540
and though I feel heavy as I leave
my floatie of a body behind,

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:20.120
I am being freed.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.410
I looked up at the bubbles

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:26.330
as I let myself sink
until my back touched the bottom.

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:31.450
Sneak, sneak, sneak, sneak...

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:34.040
Swoosh, swoosh, swoosh, swoosh...

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.290
Sneak, sneak, sneak, sneak...
Sneak, sneak, sneak, sneak...

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:42.370
Sneak, sneak, sneak...

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:43.500
Swoosh, swoosh, swoosh, swoosh...

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:44.870
Sneak, sneak, sneak, sneak...

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:57.540
Sis! Sis!

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:33.870
"Distance"

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:36.700
"I'm thinking about stopping by
your place today... You mind??!"

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:36.700
"Adachi, can you do sit-ups???"

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:38.120
"Adachi, can you do sit-ups???"

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:41.830
What even was that message just now?

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:46.870
I-It's exactly how it sounds...
I-I was wondering if you can do sit-ups.

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:48.620
Sit-ups?

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:51.160
Uh, um...

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:53.910
I mean, I just did one, but...

00:02:54.910 --> 00:03:01.370
That's amazing. You see, I can't do any
unless someone holds down my feet.

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:02.500
Seriously?

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.410
Seriously.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.620
I see...

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:07.620
Is that all?

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.580
Yup. That's it. Bye.

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:14.580
What the heck was that conversation?

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:17.080
We're leaving!

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:19.410
Yup, yup, yup, yup.

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:27.160
Man...

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.790
That was a good workout.

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:31.580
You dummy.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:35.410
Seriously? You just walked for five minutes?

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:40.330
Honestly. At least get
the most out of this trial voucher.

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:45.950
By the way, have you been
going to school every day?

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:48.410
You see me leave every day.

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:51.160
That doesn't mean
you're actually going to school.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:55.500
I-I am, though...

00:03:55.500 --> 00:04:00.250
You're the one that's going
to suffer if you don't go.

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:03.410
And the people around you.

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:10.080
I've always taught you not to be a burden
to those around you, haven't I?

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:13.620
I just said I know and left.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:15.910
Not being a burden to others

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:20.450
is the one thing my mom
had always drilled into me.

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:25.830
I'm sure she feared that I'd end up
a good-for-nothing in the future.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:28.250
Don't be a burden...

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:34.830
For example, is the fact that I'm
floating here actually burdening anyone?

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:37.160
Just like when I'm skipping school...

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:40.000
I'm just escaping being in
a classroom because it feels like

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.370
I'm stuck at the bottom of a well
and can't breathe.

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:48.370
Classes will continue even if I'm not there,
without a hitch.

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:57.750
Looking up at the water's surface,
it turned everything blue.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:02.160
It reminded of the label of
the mineral water Adachi drinks.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:05.040
It was a brilliant shade of aqua.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:08.000
Somehow, just that color and the reflections

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.540
seemed precious.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:20.200
Hiyah.

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:34.080
Seriously, how old are you?

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:36.620
I'm so happy I joined this gym...

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:41.250
I guess even I get some
excellent ideas at times.

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:44.830
I'll do it!

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:47.750
--We did that last week!
--I'll go first!

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:51.410
Yikes...

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:21.750
I don't like you.

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:24.370
This place is filled with grandpas and grandmas,

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:28.870
so even someone my age gets to enjoy
being the youngest and feeling superior.

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:31.830
And then you had to show up.

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:34.790
You understand what I'm getting at, right?

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:36.120
Sure...

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:41.290
I'm just kidding. But it is rare
to see someone young like you here.

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:43.660
I'm sure it is.

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:46.750
Oh, I didn't know you were here, Ms. Adachi.

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:48.540
Oh! Well, hello, Ms. Shimada

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:50.080
Adachi...

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:55.160
Ah... So this is destiny.

00:06:56.870 --> 00:06:59.040
Japan is tiny.

00:06:59.040 --> 00:06:59.910
--Who would've thought I'd run
into Adachi's mom in a place like this.

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:03.870
--That coach is just awful.
--Who would've thought I'd run
into Adachi's mom in a place like this.

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:04.870
--Right? The other one's so much better.
And they sound better.

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:08.000
--Adachi hates talking about her parents.
--Right? The other one's so much better.
And they sound better.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:10.620
--Her lips tighten and she never really
talks about them.
--Right? The other one's so much better.
And they sound better.

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:11.160
--You're absolutely right.
Being younger isn't everything.

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:15.200
--I don't feel any warmth in how
Adachi feels about her parents.
--You're absolutely right.
Being younger isn't everything.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:18.540
By the way, how old is your daughter now?

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:21.540
She's 15. A first-year in high school.

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:24.120
Then things must be easier
now that entrance exams are over.

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:26.080
Yes...

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:30.950
They are, but she's such a troublemaker.
I just don't know what to do with her.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:37.540
She at least goes to school,
but who knows if she's actually trying?

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:42.160
She never says what she's thinking.
I just don't get her.

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:44.200
She's such a depressing child.

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:53.910
And she's shy.

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:54.950
Excuse me.

00:07:56.750 --> 00:08:00.660
I don't... know Ada... your daughter very well,

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:03.700
but maybe you shouldn't
talk about her like that.

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:07.290
Maybe you don't understand her

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:10.000
because you haven't actually
tried to understand her.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:14.000
--Who do you--?
--I'm not trying to start an argument.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:15.790
Are you here with a parent?

00:08:15.790 --> 00:08:17.370
I am. And?

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:19.330
What's their name?

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:24.040
That really has nothing to do with this.
They're not going to talk to you.

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:29.410
I don't exactly know what's right here,

00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:32.000
so let's have a competition
to decide what's right.

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:34.200
A competition?

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:37.750
Whoever can stay in the sauna longer wins.

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:40.200
If I win, I'm right.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:44.200
So just for today, I ask that you actually
be a good mom to your daughter.

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:47.620
Is this your way of being defiant or something?

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:49.540
Pretty much.

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:57.500
I wonder how long it's been.
The ringing in my ears is getting worse.

00:08:57.500 --> 00:08:59.870
I'm sure that Adachi could never even imagine

00:08:59.870 --> 00:09:02.700
that her mom and her classmate were

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:06.830
childishly duking it out in the sauna right now.

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:11.580
So, what exactly is a good mom to you?

00:09:12.950 --> 00:09:16.790
I don't know because I've never been a mother.

00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:20.620
Just give me your ideal then.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:23.330
I think just a normal mom would be fine.

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:25.000
Normal?

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:29.500
Like being with your kid and
having dinner with them, maybe?

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:33.080
How am I supposed to know?

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:39.950
Want me to let you win?

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:42.290
You don't have to let me win.

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:43.250
Let me.

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:44.080
No.

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:45.040
I'll do it.

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:46.660
Please don't.

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:51.370
If she's actually happy...

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:56.910
If she's actually happy,
I wish she'd just tell me.

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:58.500
Are you talking about your daughter?

00:09:58.500 --> 00:09:59.750
Yes.

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:02.910
She just shuts herself off from everyone,
no matter where I take her.

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:05.870
I have no idea if she's having fun or anxious.

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:07.620
When was this?

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:10.870
She was probably five? Oh, maybe four.

00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:16.750
Why are you thinking about the past?
Why not think about your daughter now?

00:10:16.750 --> 00:10:20.500
No one likes listening
to their mother at that age.

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:22.580
I sure didn't.

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:25.450
That's true, but...

00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:27.910
Okay, I'll go ahead let you win.

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:30.040
You don't have to.

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:33.700
My daughter...

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:38.290
Ah, well. Whatever...

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:48.830
Didn't this happen before?

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:50.750
Yeah...

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:53.500
But last time, you were doing this for me.

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:55.620
Oh, right.

00:10:55.620 --> 00:10:57.080
You okay?

00:10:57.080 --> 00:11:00.250
Your legs seem to keep twitching.

00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:04.870
U-Um... Yup. It's not a big deal.

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:10.250
So yesterday... My mom was being weird.

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:13.870
She was weird?

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:16.120
We had dinner together.

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:18.200
And that's weird?

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:22.000
It's weird... and sort of nostalgic.

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:24.330
But also suffocating.

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:30.200
She always makes food for me,
but we never eat together.

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:32.620
And she's rarely ever home.

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:34.200
Did it make you happy?

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:39.910
Not really. I was so anxious that I had
no idea what the food tasted like.

00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:43.830
I wonder what all that was about though.

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:47.950
I can't say that I have a clue.

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:55.660
Y-You're c-close...

00:11:55.660 --> 00:11:57.830
Adachi... Huh?

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:01.830
S-Sorry!

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:05.410
Shimamura?

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:10.830
I guess I really can smell you...

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:14.040
H-Huh?!

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:16.830
Oh, yeah. Adachi, do some sit-ups for me.

00:12:16.830 --> 00:12:18.790
Huh? Sit-ups?

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:21.200
Two...

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:27.080
Th-Three...

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:30.160
F-Fou...

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:31.120
Fou...

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:32.080
Adachi.

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:33.450
Huh?

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:36.370
I can see up your skirt.

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:45.040
Wait, did I do something wrong?
I was just trying to warn you.

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:46.290
That's sexual harassment.

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:51.450
Oh, come on! I was the only one who saw.

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:55.000
Well, it's because that you saw
that it's... you know.

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:56.000
I do?

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:58.080
Yeah, you know...

00:13:00.290 --> 00:13:04.160
I-I guess you can't do any sit-ups, Shimamura...

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:21.080
Um... was that supposed to be a sit-up?

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:25.790
I guess nothing can ever change in just a day.

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:27.870
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:30.080
Oh, stuff.

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:31.790
"Nagafuji Butcher Shop"

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:33.250
"Nagafuji Butcher Shop"

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:33.250
Ah...

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:37.120
I noticed she seemed to be emitting the
same kind of wavelengths as you.

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:39.410
So she's your little sister.

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:42.410
Don't worry. This little weirdo is Yashiro.

00:13:42.410 --> 00:13:45.660
She's my friend, or rather...

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:47.540
It's destiny!

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:52.040
Here. A token of our friendship.

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:53.830
Would you like one?

00:13:55.870 --> 00:13:58.540
Okay.

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:00.200
You can have half, Sis.

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:01.790
Oh, sure.

00:14:05.660 --> 00:14:08.200
I've had this before...

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:15.450
You see, I'm an alien.

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:20.870
Make sure you don't believe that.

00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:24.290
Nom, nom... Yummy!

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:29.870
She's a fairy...

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:34.950
My sister ended up naming
her peculiar friend "Yachi."

00:14:35.080 --> 00:14:36.290
"Karaoke, getting something to eat,
or the river..."
"Where do you want to go???"

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:40.200
"Karaoke, getting something to eat,
or the river..."
"Where do you want to go???"

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:40.200
Uh... Shimamura? What's this message about?

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:44.500
I picked karaoke.
Nagafuji wanted to eat somewhere,

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:46.790
and Hino wanted to go to the river.

00:14:46.790 --> 00:14:52.450
Hino invited me out next Sunday,
so I figured I'd invite you, too.

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:58.200
Oh, I see... But wouldn't I make things awkward?

00:14:58.200 --> 00:15:02.200
Wait, you actually worry about stuff like that?

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:04.620
Who do you think I am?

00:15:04.620 --> 00:15:08.750
Hm... I figured you probably
didn't care about harmony.

00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:11.620
Th-That's not true...

00:15:11.620 --> 00:15:15.370
Really? Well, I guess you're coming then.

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:18.120
Uh... Sure.

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:20.200
So where do you want to go?

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:25.080
So wait, are we going to end up
going wherever I pick?

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:26.290
Probably.

00:15:26.290 --> 00:15:27.830
Is that okay?

00:15:27.830 --> 00:15:29.250
Sure.

00:15:29.250 --> 00:15:33.250
Hm... Then karaoke, I guess.

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:34.750
Okay.

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:37.620
Then I'll go ahead and tell Hino and Nagafuji.

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:40.250
Huh? Um, Shimamura...

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:45.120
Um... I...

00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:47.790
Let's-- O-Ow...

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:50.250
Uh, Adachi?

00:15:50.250 --> 00:15:53.830
Er... Let's sing something together.

00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:56.160
Sure... What should we sing?

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:59.870
Um... Something you like.

00:15:59.870 --> 00:16:02.750
Huh? Then...

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:06.290
"Post Office"

00:16:09.330 --> 00:16:13.540
You're always late to class,
but you're actually on time to hang out.

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:18.540
I'm not sure how I feel hearing that from you.

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:22.120
Blue Hair's not here today.

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:24.040
What's up?

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:30.790
Huh? H-Hey, did you buy that outfit
at Shimamura? It looks great on you!

00:16:30.790 --> 00:16:33.750
You do realize everyone makes that joke, right?

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:38.620
It would've been great if you
wore your work outfit, Adachi.

00:16:38.620 --> 00:16:40.750
Heyo!

00:16:40.750 --> 00:16:42.370
Hey.

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:45.750
I didn't think you'd actually show up, Adacchi.

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:48.410
Y-Yeah... Well, I had nothing better to do.

00:16:48.410 --> 00:16:50.410
Ah, yes. You were bored.

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:54.040
You either sound like a high school kid
or death with that motive, so I approve.

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:56.870
Adacchi, let's totes have fun today.

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:58.830
Yeah, Adacchi.

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:02.370
Adacchi.

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:05.790
Okay, I guess I'll get things started.

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:08.250
♪ The void of time... ♪

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:10.500
Stop that.

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:12.660
Okay, I guess I'll actually put in a song.

00:17:12.660 --> 00:17:14.410
"Song Requests"

00:17:12.660 --> 00:17:14.410
I can't get used to this.

00:17:14.410 --> 00:17:15.580
I can't get used to this.

00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:16.790
"Dandelion"

00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:16.790
I can't get used to this.

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:22.330
I don't mind having fun with everyone
like this, but something feels off.

00:17:22.330 --> 00:17:24.620
And it also seems like Shimamura

00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:28.830
is forcing herself to do this.

00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:33.160
Thinking back on her in a daze
on the second floor of the gym...

00:17:33.160 --> 00:17:35.620
That seemed more normal.

00:17:36.870 --> 00:17:40.580
Even though Shimamura and I have
the difference of being good or bad at it,

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:44.870
I think we pretty much feel the same
when it comes to hanging out with people.

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:47.870
And the fact that we're so similar with that

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:49.080
makes me...

00:17:50.910 --> 00:17:52.450
Here!

00:17:52.450 --> 00:17:54.250
You can go next.

00:17:56.370 --> 00:18:00.580
Well, if we're going in order, it should be you.

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:02.580
Okay.

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:04.200
Could I get another mic?

00:18:05.870 --> 00:18:10.200
Ta-da! Adachi and I are going to sing together!

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:11.250
Here's your mic.

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:12.950
Yeah! Adacchi!

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:14.250
Adacchi!

00:18:14.250 --> 00:18:16.370
"Song Name: <i>Merry-go-round</i>"
"Send"

00:18:16.750 --> 00:18:20.410
Um... Shimamura?

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:23.120
You'd be helping me out if you sang with me.

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:24.950
Huh?

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:28.450
I don't like singing in front of people.

00:18:31.660 --> 00:18:36.120
I'm glad I'm with you, too.

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:42.790
<i>Round and round goes the merry-go-round</i>

00:18:42.790 --> 00:18:47.410
<i>I want to reach you, but I just can't</i>

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:52.290
<i>Will there ever be a day that we'll overlap?</i>

00:18:52.290 --> 00:18:57.950
<i>I hope you feel the same way, too...</i>

00:19:04.500 --> 00:19:12.580
<i>It's like the middle of a donut</i>

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:20.330
<i>You think there's something there,</i>
<i>but it's nowhere to be found</i>

00:19:20.330 --> 00:19:25.950
<i>The sweeter it gets, the more I want to peek</i>

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:36.040
<i>The moment I casually got on board,</i>
<i>the bell rings</i>

00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:37.830
<i>I stared at you</i>

00:19:37.830 --> 00:19:39.870
<i>I was just staring off into the distance</i>

00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:42.750
<i>Because we'll get dizzy</i>

00:19:42.750 --> 00:19:45.700
<i>All sparkly and all fluffy, we get closer</i>

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:47.620
Did you have fun, Adacchi?

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:51.620
Uh... I'd rather you just say my name normally.

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:55.410
You don't like nicknames?
Wait, why am I the only one not allowed?

00:19:55.410 --> 00:19:58.700
That's not what I meant...

00:19:58.700 --> 00:20:00.910
So, how was it?

00:20:00.910 --> 00:20:02.080
It was okay.

00:20:03.700 --> 00:20:05.700
Hey, turn right.

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:08.580
Wait, isn't your house to the left?

00:20:08.580 --> 00:20:10.500
Just do it.

00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:17.950
<i>But how do you feel about me?</i>

00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:21.080
They didn't have your usual mineral water.

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:22.660
Thanks...

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:27.750
It's nice and breezy near your house.

00:20:27.750 --> 00:20:30.250
Isn't the view amazing, too?

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:36.370
You don't like doing stuff like that, do you?

00:20:36.370 --> 00:20:41.200
Huh? Um... maybe.

00:20:41.200 --> 00:20:43.700
I won't invite you anymore if you don't like it.

00:20:43.700 --> 00:20:47.950
It's okay. I'm not suffering or anything,
so please invite me again.

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:49.370
Okay.

00:20:53.950 --> 00:20:55.040
And?

00:20:58.750 --> 00:21:03.870
Well... it seemed like you had
something you wanted to talk about.

00:21:03.870 --> 00:21:06.910
You kept looking at me at karaoke.

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:09.040
Huh?!

00:21:09.040 --> 00:21:11.160
Was I staring that hard?

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:12.080
Yup.

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:14.370
I-I think you were just imagining it.

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:17.200
Our eyes met so many times.

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:22.200
I have a bunch of things
I want to say to Shimamura...

00:21:22.200 --> 00:21:25.450
But if I said any of them,
I feel like she'd look at me weird,

00:21:25.450 --> 00:21:27.580
or she'd run away...

00:21:27.580 --> 00:21:31.700
They're all things like that,
so I just shrink back.

00:21:31.700 --> 00:21:34.790
And they just keep piling up...
and become stagnate.

00:21:34.790 --> 00:21:38.870
I feel like a bunch of things
just dog-pile above my neck.

00:21:38.870 --> 00:21:41.950
Like when a fruit ripens and gathers nutrients,

00:21:41.950 --> 00:21:45.660
but after some time,
it rots and falls to the ground.

00:21:45.660 --> 00:21:47.580
That's how it felt.

00:21:47.580 --> 00:21:50.160
Just like a sapling sticking out of the ground,

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:54.620
the end peeks out and tries to escape my mouth.

00:21:54.620 --> 00:21:57.790
I held it back, but I was too late.

00:22:00.790 --> 00:22:02.540
Shimamura.

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:08.290
Could you pat me on the head?

00:22:11.750 --> 00:22:14.330
I can't even look up anymore.

00:22:16.250 --> 00:22:18.000
Hm.

00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:20.040
I overcame these feelings of regrets mixed

00:22:20.040 --> 00:22:22.500
with something else many times and despaired.

00:22:22.500 --> 00:22:25.410
But then, I still looked forward.

00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:40.080
I guess you like being coddled, Adachi.

00:22:40.080 --> 00:22:41.450
How's that?

00:22:41.450 --> 00:22:43.080
Just a bit more...

00:22:45.120 --> 00:22:51.200
It felt like time and the Earth had just
come to a stop and were staring at us.

00:22:51.200 --> 00:22:53.290
Despite how fast my heart was beating,

00:22:53.290 --> 00:22:58.250
my heart was so calm
I almost wanted to cry softly.

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:02.370
I'm so happy right now from a girl
from my class patting me on the head.

00:23:02.370 --> 00:23:07.580
What's with me? Am I stupid? Am I weird?

00:23:07.580 --> 00:23:10.500
I'm sure it's actually a little bit of both...

00:23:13.330 --> 00:23:15.250
Is that enough?

00:23:15.250 --> 00:23:17.330
Yeah...

00:23:17.330 --> 00:23:20.910
Don't call me Big Sis in class, okay?

00:23:20.910 --> 00:23:24.370
Oh, give me your can.
I'll go throw it away for you.

00:23:27.330 --> 00:23:30.080
Oh, there's still some left.

00:23:30.080 --> 00:23:31.370
Oh, okay.

00:23:33.950 --> 00:23:38.910
I lied. The can was actually empty.

00:23:41.330 --> 00:23:44.250
I want to be someone special to Shimamura.

00:23:45.200 --> 00:23:47.290
I don't mean that in a weird way.

00:23:47.290 --> 00:23:49.870
But if I actually was special to her,

00:23:49.870 --> 00:23:52.040
I don't care if it's weird.

00:23:52.040 --> 00:23:52.450
"Episode 4: 'High School Girls On Holiday'"

00:23:52.450 --> 00:23:56.660
"Episode 4: 'High School Girls On Holiday'"

00:23:52.450 --> 00:23:56.660
I came to the realization
that I guess I really do like her.

00:23:56.660 --> 00:23:57.950
"Episode 4: 'High School Girls On Holiday'"

00:23:57.950 --> 00:24:00.660
"Next Time: 'Adachi's Question'"

00:23:57.950 --> 00:24:00.660
Adashimapedia: Karaoke!

00:24:00.660 --> 00:24:03.160
"Next Time: 'Adachi's Question'"

00:24:00.660 --> 00:24:03.160
That moment when you're singing your
heart out and the employee comes in.

00:24:03.160 --> 00:24:04.370
"Next Time: 'Adachi's Question'"

00:24:03.160 --> 00:24:04.370
Clack. Pardon me!

00:24:04.370 --> 00:24:06.750
Wait! The real employee just showed up!

00:24:06.750 --> 00:24:08.950
--Er, I...
--Wow, it's the real deal!

00:24:08.950 --> 00:24:11.160
--Seriously...
--It's the employee, Hino!

00:24:11.160 --> 00:24:12.620
That was your point?!
